# The GeoSPARQL 1.1 requirement census, authored in-house from OGC 22-047r1 (no upstream
# conformance-test manifest exists for GeoSPARQL 1.1). One entry per normative requirement id,
# 57 in total across the seven conformance classes. Every entry carries the arm's disposition:
# "decided" (live conformance rows exercise the requirement, named in arm:evidence),
# "pinned-backlog" (not yet decided; arm:reason names what the decision awaits; none at present), or
# "silenced-with-reason" (deliberately out of the claimed scope; none at present).
# The coverage ledger in Geo/GeoConformanceCoverageTests.cs asserts this census is total:
# 57 unique ids, the per-class totals, and a closed disposition set — zero invisible complement.

PREFIX arm: <urn:x-veritas:geosparql-arm#>

# Core — /conf/core (7 requirement ids).

[] arm:requirement "/req/core/sparql-protocol" ;
   arm:conformanceClass "core" ;
   arm:bucket "other" ;
   arm:disposition "decided" ;
   arm:evidence "The serve command's HTTP endpoint is the engine's SPARQL 1.1 Protocol endpoint under the server deployment posture - the embedded and decentralized postures share the engine surface beneath it. Query evaluation answers all four query forms at the database facade, pinned by the Tests-project Database/VeritasEngineQueryFormsTests battery - CONSTRUCT instantiation with fresh per-solution blank nodes, DESCRIBE as the Concise Bounded Description over explicit IRIs, bound variables, star, and the absent resource, the engine-default store-local graph source with its typed unknown-graph refusal, the protocol-dataset override, and the options-resolver override. The protocol's query operation is served whole, pinned by the Tests-project Cli/VeritasCliIntegrationTests battery - the three submission forms (ServeCommandAnswersHttpQuery, ServeCommandAnswersHttpPostQuery, ServeCommandAnswersUrlEncodedFormPostQuery), content negotiation across the SPARQL Query Results XML and JSON serializations and the delimited formats (ServeCommandNegotiatesSparqlResultsXml, ServeCommandNegotiatesTheDelimitedFormats), ASK answering a real results document in JSON and XML (ServeCommandAnswersAskAsResultsJsonAndXml), graph results as N-Triples and Turtle including under a tabular Accept (ServeCommandAnswersConstructAsNTriplesAndTurtle, ServeCommandAnswersConstructUnderATabularAccept), the dataset parameters selecting the loaded named graphs and refusing an unknown IRI by name (ServeCommandSelectsTheNamedGraphThroughProtocolDataset, ServeCommandRefusesAnUnknownDatasetGraph), the malformed-400/refused-500 fault split (ServeCommandSplitsProtocolFaults), the 415 content-type refusal (ServeCommandRefusesAnUnknownPostContentType), and the SPARQL 1.1 Service Description on a query-less GET (ServeCommandServesTheServiceDescription)." .

[] arm:requirement "/req/core/spatial-object-class" ;
   arm:conformanceClass "core" ;
   arm:bucket "vocabulary" ;
   arm:disposition "decided" ;
   arm:evidence "Geo/GeoVocabularyGraphPatternTests.ClassIsUsableInGraphPatterns binds the typed member through a rdf:type graph pattern over geo:SpatialObject and leaves the decoy unmatched." .

[] arm:requirement "/req/core/feature-class" ;
   arm:conformanceClass "core" ;
   arm:bucket "vocabulary" ;
   arm:disposition "decided" ;
   arm:evidence "Geo/GeoVocabularyGraphPatternTests.ClassIsUsableInGraphPatterns binds the typed member through a rdf:type graph pattern over geo:Feature and leaves the decoy unmatched; the feature-geometry-serialization join row exercises the class inside a three-pattern query." .

